        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "0d6f1836-25d3-59e9-80dd-daa152c40b95",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Gordon Waller, Paul McCartney, Norman Newell, Del Davis\n- Groups: Peter and Gordon, Lennon–McCartney\n- Songs: \"A World Without Love\", \"World Without Love\"\n- Albums: \"Mellow Dubmarine\"\n- Companies: EMI\n\nFacts:\n- Gordon Waller was born on 4 June 1945 and died on 17 July 2009.\n- Gordon Waller was a British singer-songwriter-guitarist.\n- Gordon Waller was best known as Gordon in the 1960s pop duo Peter and Gordon.\n- Peter and Gordon had a No. 1 million-selling hit with \"A World Without Love.\"\n- Paul McCartney wrote \"A World Without Love,\" and the song was credited to Lennon–McCartney.\n- Norman Newell worked as an A&R manager for EMI.\n- At EMI, Norman Newell worked with Peter and Gordon as well as artists including Shirley Bassey, Claude François, Vera Lynn, Russ Conway, Bette Midler, Judy Garland, Petula Clark, Jake Thackray, Malcolm Roberts, and Bobby Crush.\n- Del Davis recorded a cover of \"World Without Love\" that was featured on \"Mellow Dubmarine\".",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
